# fixedbugs, defect 151, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R3), the
# completeness critic's `cov_zero`.
#
# SYMPTOM: `SZ { kind; union { int32_t i; float f; }; }` bound by `kind` and
# `f`, which covers its union, compared two values whose `i` is `INT32_MIN`
# and `0` as `true`: `f` reads `-0.0` and `0.0`, which a float compares equal.
#
# FIX: a float arm is not compared bit for bit, so a record holding one in a
# union is not compared at all, however wide the arm. Reading `f` and building
# an `SZ` that names it stay legal.

extern "fixedbugs-151-unions.h"
    record SZ  #~ ffi_union_field
        kind: i32
        f: f32

function same(x: SZ, y: SZ) -> bool
    return x == y

function main()
    print(1)
